course: dictionary
lesson: 12067
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word cleaners can mean people, things, or a shop. The words around it tell you which meaning fits, and those words are the context.
explain: «The school cleaners arrive at six o'clock to mop the floors.» Here cleaners are people, because they arrive and do a job. «I bought a new bottle of floor cleaner for the kitchen.» Here cleaners are a product that you use for cleaning.
explain: «Mum took her coat to the cleaners.» Here the cleaners is a shop that cleans clothes with special chemicals. Ask yourself: is it a person, a thing, or a place? Then check that your choice makes sense in the sentence.
fact: Cleaners is the plural of cleaner, and it can be a noun for people, products, or shops.
fact: Cleaners are people whose job is to clean buildings, like schools, offices or homes.
fact: Cleaners can also be products or machines used for cleaning, such as floor cleaners or vacuum cleaners.
fact: «The cleaners» or «the dry cleaner's» can mean a shop that cleans clothes.
fact: Household cleaners, like bleach and oven cleaner, are poisonous. Never drink, sniff or mix them, and keep each one in its own bottle.
exercise: «The school cleaners keep our classrooms clean.» Who are the cleaners in this sentence? | *People whose job is to clean the school | A machine that sucks up dust | A shop that cleans clothes
exercise: «Dad bought a new bottle of oven cleaner.» What kind of cleaners are these? | People who work in an office | *Products used for cleaning | A dry-cleaning shop
exercise: «Mum took her wool jumper to the cleaner's.» What does the cleaner's mean here? | A bottle of bleach | A person who cleans schools | *A shop that cleans clothes with special chemicals
test: «Never mix bleach with other cleaners, because it can make a dangerous gas.» Why must you never mix cleaners? | It makes the bottle too heavy | It makes the floor too shiny to walk on | It will smell of flowers | *It can make a dangerous gas
test: «The window cleaners came on Monday and made the glass sparkle.» Are the window cleaners people, products or a shop? | A product, because it made the glass sparkle | *People, because they came and did the work | A shop, because it came on Monday
exam: «Ben's dad was taken to the cleaners when a bad deal lost him a lot of money.» What does be taken to the cleaners mean? | Given a job at the dry cleaner's | *Lost a lot of money | Told off for being messy | Cleaned from head to toe
